From: Second Chapter
Subject: [PATCH] drm/grate: fbdev: use XBGR8888 so KOReader colours are right

KOReader writes red in the lowest byte and its EPUB renderer cannot swap
channels, so on XRGB8888 red and blue appeared swapped. The Tegra display
supports XBGR8888 and the console reads the bitfields, so use that.
(The grate kernel builds drivers/gpu/drm/grate, not drivers/gpu/drm/tegra.)

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/fbdev.c	2026-11-25 12:13:28.153111631 +0000
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/fbdev.c	2026-11-25 12:13:28.210155942 +0000
@@ -92,6 +92,15 @@
 
 	cmd.pixel_format = drm_mode_legacy_fb_format(sizes->surface_bpp,
 						     sizes->surface_depth);
+	/*
+	 * Second Chapter: use red-green-blue byte order (XBGR8888) rather
+	 * than the usual XRGB8888, as KOReader draws straight to the
+	 * framebuffer in that order, and its EPUB renderer can't swap red and
+	 * blue itself. The display supports both; the text console reads the
+	 * order from the framebuffer settings, so it's unaffected.
+	 */
+	if (cmd.pixel_format == DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888)
+		cmd.pixel_format = DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888;
 
 	size = cmd.pitches[0] * cmd.height;
 
